-- The GHC HEAD half of Run 19: the same source, shim and roster as
-- cabal.project on a compiler no released freeze can name. Select it with
-- --project-file=cabal.project.ghead; cabal.project.ghead.freeze beside it
-- pins the resolved plan as cabal.project.freeze and cabal.project.ghc914.freeze
-- pin theirs, at the same index-state, so the three plans differ in the boot
-- libraries and in nothing else a freeze can see.
--
-- cabal.project.freeze pins base ==4.21.2.0 and so refuses every other
-- compiler, which is why HEAD wants a project file of its own. The constraints
-- below are what the resolver needs before a freeze exists, and are kept here
-- rather than left to the freeze because a freeze is regenerated and these are
-- decisions: `base installed` takes the compiler's own boot base; vector and
-- criterion are pinned at the versions every run in this README was taken on,
-- vector with the +boundschecks -unsafechecks that makes the gen-quotrem
-- against gen-unsafe pair price a bounds check at all; and hashable needs
-- naming outright, 1.5.1.0's cabal file not declaring the ghc-bignum its
-- source imports, where 1.5.0.0's does. head.hackage is neither needed nor
-- helpful -- its index here is stale enough that the tarball hashes no longer
-- verify.
--
-- The compiler is the in-tree stage1 of the GHC checkout under
-- ~/r/horde-ad/ghc, at 10.1.20260803. Its path is spelled out because there is
-- no such compiler on PATH; a HEAD that moves is a different compiler and a
-- different pair, so a run repeating this one reads the version back out of the
-- binary rather than off this line.
packages: .
with-compiler: /home/mikolaj/r/horde-ad/ghc/_build/stage1/bin/ghc
index-state: hackage.haskell.org 2026-07-25T13:22:10Z

allow-newer: base, ghc-prim, ghc-bignum, template-haskell,
             deepseq, bytestring, containers, text, time

constraints: base installed,
             criterion ==1.6.5.0,
             vector ==0.13.2.0,
             vector +boundschecks -unsafechecks,
             hashable ==1.5.0.0
